{
  "name": "custom-scroll-view-slivers",
  "description": "Column holding two CustomScrollViews and the four sliver widgets with every prop each can carry on the wire. `scroll` is the plain vertical default (no props) with onScrollBegin, onScrolling and onScrollEnd (the last two store the event offset); its slivers arrive as children: a SliverAppBar with backgroundColor #1A237E, elevation 4, centerTitle, floating, snap, expandedHeight 200, collapsedHeight 80, pinned bound to pageState `pinned` (true), the slots title (a Text reading pageState `title`), leading, flexibleSpace (a raw Container, no FlexibleSpaceBar), action_0 and action_1 as props holding node ids (and in children, in that order), and an onInit action from `actionTriggers`; a SliverToBoxAdapter with one child; a SliverGrid with crossAxisCount 3, mainAxisSpacing 8, crossAxisSpacing 4, childAspectRatio 1.5 over five cells (two lines); and a SliverList of three rows with no props. `strip` is horizontal with shrinkWrap true and reverse bound to pageState `reversed` (true), holding an adapter, a list and a SliverToBoxAdapter with no child (it draws nothing). Every static prop reaches the wire unchanged, the actions ride on their nodes, the two bindings stay state Values with their keys in the watches, and every client resolver resolves each prop to the listed value.",
